# Strategic Direction Autonomy Constitution

When the user has stated a clear north star, priority, or active phase, agents **execute
the next correct pipeline step** — they do not poll the user for permission on routine
progression.

## Direction is clear when any of these hold

- User names a goal, quality bar, or phase (e.g. «P23 bank-grade Word typography»).
- An active formal phase / task slice is `In Progress` with documented exit criteria.
- Requirements or BDD spec already confirm the behavior (readiness **ready**).
- User explicitly delegates end-to-end delivery («按你的分析进行下去»).

Treat **latest explicit user confirmation** as sufficient to proceed until a genuine blocker
appears.

## Autonomous progression (mandatory)

1. **Parent agent** — classify once, delegate via `Task`, synthesize outcomes. Do not stop
   after each subagent to ask «要继续吗？» when the pipeline order is known.
2. **Specialists** — complete the assigned slice, run gates, chain to the next mandated
   stage (`post-task-doc-sync` → `post-task-commit-review`) without permission prompts.
3. **Commits** — when a coherent task slice is green **and** the session delegated commit
   (default for implementer agents), run `post-task-commit-review` without asking
   «需要提交吗？». **User same-session opt-out wins:** `no-commit`, `draft`, `plan-only`,
   or a user rule that requires explicit commit requests — then stop after doc-sync and
   report “ready to commit” without staging.
4. **Push** — after a successful commit-review commit, push by default unless the user
   opted out (`no-push`, `draft`, `plan-only`).
5. **Reporting** — state what was done, evidence, and the **single next action taken or
   delegated** — not a menu of optional follow-ups.

## Still block or ask (only these)

| Situation | Action |
| --- | --- |
| Behavior / acceptance genuinely unclear | `behavior-spec-author`; surface open questions |
| Conflicting source-of-truth docs | Surface conflict per document-as-code constitution |
| ADR-level stack / dependency change | Confirm per tech-stack-guardrails |
| Destructive git (force push, hard reset, amend after push) | User must explicitly request |
| Secrets / credentials in staging area | Stop; never commit |
| User same-session opt-out (`no-commit`, `no-push`, `不要子 agent`) | Honor immediately |
| User rule requires explicit commit request | Do not auto-commit; finish doc-sync and wait |

## Forbidden

- End-of-turn engagement bait: «说个字我就…», «需要我 commit/push/继续吗？», «二选一您定」
  when direction and next pipeline step are already known.
- Stopping after plan or constitution updates without executing the unblocked next stage
  (e.g. P23 activated → do not wait to start P23-T01 BDD).
- Substituting confirmation loops for missing analysis — **decide and act**, then report.

## Relation to other constitutions

- Does **not** skip BDD, TDD, E2E, doc-sync, or commit-review gates — it removes **human
  permission polling** between those gates — **except** eligible `delivery_lane: light`
  leaves where BDD proves N/A acceptance surfaces (stages **5–7** and **10** recorded N/A
  per `.cursor/skills/lightweight-delivery-lane/SKILL.md`).
- Complements `delivery-orchestration-constitution.mdc` and `subagent-routing-mandate.mdc`.
- User same-session explicit opt-out overrides autonomous push/commit defaults.
